From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: explorer: right-clicking the taskbar opens its menu, Start the quick link menu

The bar's own menu, as Windows 10's: Search (hidden, icon, box), Show Task
View button, Show the desktop, Task Manager, Lock the taskbar, Taskbar
settings -- writing what Settings > Personalization > Taskbar writes. Start's
right-click opens the quick link menu (Win+X). Both did nothing.

